#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:110
msgid "None"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:122
msgid ""
"Accepts ``None`` (a surface representation), a name "
"from :data:`REPRESENTATION_TYPES`, or a representation class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:129
msgid ""
"*color* is either a 3-sequence with components in ``[0, 1]`` or a snake_case "
"named color from :mod:`vtkmodules.util.colors` (e.g. ``\"tomato\"``, "
"``\"steel_blue\"``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:136
msgid ""
"The override classes below add properties of their own -- named colors, and "
"anything reached by delegation -- that the wrapped class knows nothing "
"about.  Deciding what VTK's own constructor handling will accept has to ask "
"that class, not this one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:143
msgid ""
"Attribute assignment on a Python subclass of a VTK object quietly creates an "
"instance attribute, which would turn a misspelled keyword argument into a "
"property that silently does nothing.  Keyword arguments are checked here so "
"that they fail where the mistake was made."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:151
msgid ""
"The C++ classes carry only what it takes to make data visible and legible; "
"everything else lives on the actor, property, mapper or filter underneath. "
"That is the right shape for C++, where reaching one object further is a "
"method call, but it would spoil ``view.show(src, specular=0.3)`` in Python, "
"where flat keyword arguments are the whole point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:157
msgid ""
"So an attribute this class does not define is looked for on each delegate in "
"turn, and set on the first that has it.  ``rep.specular = 0.3`` and "
"``rep.property.specular = 0.3`` are then the same thing, and an attribute "
"nobody owns still fails, naming the delegates it looked in."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:151
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:198
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:419
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:500
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:542
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:576
#: ../../../api/python/vtkmodules/vtkmodules.util.views_scivis.md:666
msgid "Initialization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:155
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:202
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:504
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:546
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:580
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:670
msgid "Accept in the constructor everything assignment accepts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:157
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:204
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:506
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:548
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:582
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:672
msgid ""
"VTK builds its own constructor keyword handling from the properties a class "
"declares, and it runs before any Python attribute assignment -- so it never "
"reaches the delegation below, and ``view.specular = 0.3`` would work while "
"``Class(specular=0.3)`` did not.  Anything VTK does not recognise is applied "
"here instead, which puts the two back in step."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:163
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:210
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:512
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:554
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:588
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:678
msgid ""
"A dict value configures the sub-object of that name, so the grouping the C++ "
"API has is available at construction too::"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:166
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:213
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:515
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:557
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:591
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:681
msgid ""
"view = vtkScivisView(\n"
"    window_title=\"demo\",\n"
"    selector={\"mode\": \"frustum\"},\n"
"    light_kit={\"key_light_intensity\": 0.8},\n"
")\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:172
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:219
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:521
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:563
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:597
#: ../../../../../Wrapping/Python/vtkmodules/util/views_scivis.py:687
msgid ""
"There is no way to spell that as a keyword name -- ``selector.mode=`` is a "
"syntax error -- and a dict means nothing to an ordinary VTK property, so "
"there is nothing for it to collide with."
msgstr ""

